            <div xml:id="d934">

                <pb facs="0865" n="857" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg857"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102 Tientsin/691: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tientsin</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-21T13:00:00+09:00">June 21, 1940—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>97. Barriers surrounding foreign Concessions in Tientsin removed at 6 p.m.
                    yesterday and pedestrian and vehicular traffic moved freely thereafter. Although
                    Japanese sentries were not at their usual posts, Japanese soldiers remain,
                    reputedly to ascertain the volume of traffic during coming week.</p>
                <p>Restrictions on river traffic are also understood to have been removed, vessels
                    no longer being required to stop for Japanese military inspection at Dairen
                    Kisen Kaisha wharf. Details of British municipal <pb facs="0866" n="858"
                        xml:id="pg858"/> police inspection of ship’s passengers and crews at
                    Concession wharves have not yet been worked out and at present such inspection
                    is waived.</p>
                <p>Unidentified sources state that Federal Reserve Bank will occupy its present
                    quarters (formerly in the blockaded area) in the first special area beginning
                    June 24th.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking, Peiping. Air mail to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
